From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Segno floor-console <to.sasovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: skip SYNC_APPLPTR for implicit-feedback
 sinks

lowlatency=1 advertises SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR on playback open so
the lowlatency_playback URB path sees precise appl_ptr updates. Implicit-
feedback sinks never enter that path (lowlatency_playback_available
returns false — they use the capture-driven ready-list instead), so the
flag is spurious for them.

On Focusrite Scarlett 4i4 Gen 3 (1235:8212) under linux-raspberrypi
6.18 + PREEMPT_RT, that spurious flag produces robotic monitor audio at
96 kHz / 64 frames. Disabling the module lowlatency option clears the
symptom but also disables the real lowlatency path for other devices.
Gate SYNC_APPLPTR on !JOINT_DUPLEX instead (JOINT_DUPLEX is set only for
implicit_fb formats in this driver).

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 sound/usb/pcm.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/usb/pcm.c b/sound/usb/pcm.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/sound/usb/pcm.c
+++ b/sound/usb/pcm.c
@@ -1248,10 +1248,6 @@ static int snd_usb_pcm_open(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	}
 
 	runtime->hw = snd_usb_hardware;
-	/* need an explicit sync to catch applptr update in low-latency mode */
-	if (direction == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
-	    as->chip->lowlatency)
-		runtime->hw.info |= SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR;
 	runtime->private_data = subs;
 	subs->pcm_substream = substream;
 	/* runtime PM is also done there */
@@ -1264,6 +1260,16 @@ static int snd_usb_pcm_open(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	ret = setup_hw_info(runtime, subs);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_open;
+	/* need an explicit sync to catch applptr update in low-latency mode.
+	 * Implicit-feedback sinks never use lowlatency_playback; advertising
+	 * SYNC_APPLPTR for them confuses userspace (robotic monitor on
+	 * Scarlett Gen3 @ 96 kHz / short periods). JOINT_DUPLEX is set in
+	 * setup_hw_info only when a format has implicit_fb.
+	 */
+	if (direction == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
+	    as->chip->lowlatency &&
+	    !(runtime->hw.info & SNDRV_PCM_INFO_JOINT_DUPLEX))
+		runtime->hw.info |= SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR;
 	ret = snd_usb_autoresume(subs->stream->chip);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_open;
-- 
